# Vendored reference repos — read-only, not ours to track
examples/
# Re-measurement output. The committed measurement is written only with
# F2A_RECORD_MEASUREMENTS=1; an ordinary privileged run writes .latest.json so
# it cannot silently replace a recorded figure.
tests/batteries/results/*.latest.json
# Per-run copies of the record above, written by
# `tools/removal_proofs_summary.py::_archive` so a run that disagreed with its
# neighbours is still readable. Records of runs, never committed figures — same
# rule as the line above. ~40KB a run, which is why the directory is ignored
# rather than tracked.
#
# Written as `dir/*` rather than `dir/` so a single record can be exempted
# below. The two are equivalent for everything else, and the directory form
# cannot be narrowed at all: git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so a `!` line under `dir/` would never be consulted.
tests/batteries/results/removal-proofs-history/*
# The one exemption, and it is an EXHIBIT rather than a figure. This record is
# the artifact finding 032 is *about*: it scores `T065 wiring` as `proved` in a
# run that completed with 0 unproven, on a tree where that arm's tampered test
# could not return at all. Nothing quotes a measurement out of it; it is here so
# the finding's central claim can be checked against the file rather than taken
# on the finding's word, and so the only copy stops living on one laptop.
#
# It is self-verifying: `_archive` names each record with the first 12 hex
# digits of the SHA-256 of its own bytes, so
#   python3 -c 'import hashlib;print(hashlib.sha256(open(P,"rb").read()).hexdigest()[:12])'
# must reproduce the suffix in the filename.
#
# Do not extend this to the directory. One exhibit is evidence; every run is the
# accumulation the ignore exists to prevent.
!tests/batteries/results/removal-proofs-history/removal-proofs-20260805T215946-4479acefc95f.json

# CI scratch. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` writes these into the workspace so it
# can upload them as artifacts; they are readings of one run and are never
# committed. Listed rather than written to a temp directory because
# `actions/upload-artifact` reads paths relative to the workspace.
/preflight.txt
/pytest-collected.txt
/pytest-privileged.xml
/pytest-unprivileged.xml
/privileged-suite-identity.json
/proof-attribution.txt
src/proxy/go-test.txt

# `tests/invariants/runner.py` writes this to count outcomes per invariant.
# The runner's own exit code carries the verdict; the report is scratch.
tests/invariants/.invariants-report.xml
